{"name":"Altar Wine","hex":"#5f1a10","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"altar wine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A particular type of wine produced for ritual consumption during the Roman Catholic Mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altar_wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sacramental wine","blocks":[{"text":"Sacramental wine, Communion wine, altar wine, or wine for consecration is wine obtained from grapes and intended for use in celebration of the Eucharist and the blood of Christ. It is usually consumed after sacramental bread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg/330px-US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacramental_wine","wikidata":"Q958011"},{"title":"Altar","blocks":[{"text":"An altar is a table or platform for the presentation of religious offerings, for sacrifices, or for other ritualistic purposes. Altars are found at shrines, temples, churches, and other places of worship. They are used particularly in Christianity, Buddhism, Hinduism, and modern paganism. Many historical-medieval faiths also made use of them, including the Roman, Greek, and Norse religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/RD_alter.jpg/330px-RD_alter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altar","wikidata":"Q101687"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg/500px-US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg/1280px-US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg/500px-US_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chaplain pouring sacramental wine from a cruet into a chalice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_Navy_100912-M-2275H-196_A_command_chaplain_holds_church_services_aboard_USS_Kearsarge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/St_Michael_the_Archangel%2C_Fin